    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0377" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg279"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Wu Ting-fang.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic">July 18,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr.</hi> Wu: In reference to your inquiry made
                    this morning on behalf of the Grand Secretary Li Hung Chang, I have the honor to
                    reply that the position and the intention of the United States Government in
                    favor of the territorial and administrative integrity of China are set forth
                    with sufficient clearness in our circular of the 3d of July,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d301-f1"/> that we still hold the same attitude, and that we have
                    ground to believe that similar views are entertained by all the other
                    powers.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
